scope: Decompose the 1229-line money-path god-file src/charon/proxy_server.py into 4 new modules
  behind a slim facade, so the 9 post-dedup proxy_server.py tickets stop serializing on one file and
  split into 2 parallel module-lanes (routing ‖ console). See fleet/scratch/proxy-decomposition-analysis.md
  (§2 seams, §3 owns-map, §4 blast-radius). Behavior-preserving verbatim moves ONLY — NO logic change
  in any move commit. The 4-module split (per §2/§3):
    1. proxy_console_assets.py  <- seam A (HTML string constants _CONSOLE_HTML/_WORK_HTML/_SETUP_HTML,
       ~lines 83-332, ~250 lines pure static data).
    2. proxy_response.py        <- seam B (_extract, _pre_flight_estimate, _pre_flight_pricing,
       ~lines 335-394, module-level pure functions).
    3. console_router.py        <- seam E control-plane (first half of _handle: loopback guard, token
       gate, /v1/models, /charon/status|cost, console HTML, /charon/setup + config POST-writes/CSRF,
       /charon/work; ~lines 551-686). Exposes try_handle_control_plane(handler, srv) -> bool.
    4. forwarder.py             <- seam F data-plane failover loop (second half of _handle, ~688-982)
       + seam D request build (_build_upstream_req, ~502-549). Exposes forward_with_failover(handler,
       srv, ...). HIGH-RISK step (SR-1/SR-2/DTC scar tissue) — adversarial review HERE.
  KEEP on proxy_server.py: GatewayProxyServer (seam G, routing state + _cooldown + _cooldown_lock —
  unsplit; forwarder calls through srv, never re-implements locking) + the _ProxyHandler shell and
  shared emit/auth helpers (seam C: _json/_html/_authorized/_maybe_set_token_cookie/_write/_drain/
  _send_resp_headers). _handle collapses to: loopback/token gate -> if console_router.try_handle_
  control_plane(): return -> forwarder.forward_with_failover().
  FACADE (mandatory): proxy_server.py re-exports the public surface so all 13 importing test files stay
  green with zero import edits: GatewayProxyServer, UpstreamRoute, _CONSOLE_HTML, _SETUP_HTML, _extract,
  _pre_flight_estimate (also _WORK_HTML). ARCH: add ALL 4 new modules to _ENGINE_FORBIDDEN in
  tests/test_check_arch.py (or the engine-import guard weakens — required, not optional).
  STAGING: 4 behavior-preserving verbatim-move commits, hardest last — assets -> response ->
  console_router -> forwarder; the FULL suite (PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest -q) green after EACH
  commit; no logic change may ride along in a move commit. After the move, rebase PFF Phase-1's small
  diff (trivial). Product must ship STANDALONE — no fleet/SLOP/rig dependency may leak in.
note: PARKED. Land PFF Phase-1 first (bleed-stopper on the current file), THEN this decompose, THEN
  the 2 parallel lanes (Wave C). PFF Phase-2 (money-path cross-tier substitution) lands AFTER decompose,
